Python reader
This file is a Thue++ reader. It turns a small Python program into an AST dump.
It does not evaluate the program. Strings are protected, then the rest is lexed and parsed.
Numbers keep their source spelling. Unsupported forms and broken syntax exit with a named error.
A newline ends a statement. The supported source is what ruff format emits: four spaces of indent, and no tabs. A tab is rejected.
A newline inside parentheses, or after an operator that still needs a value, is whitespace.
Precedence, low to high: or, and, not, comparison, + -, * /, unary + -. A call is postfix.
and and or chains collapse into one BoolOp. Parentheses keep a nested BoolOp.
def takes simple names. return, calls, and boolean operators are nodes, not actions.

PCT <- (?:[A-Za-z0-9_.-]|%[0-9A-F]{2})*
GOOD <- (?:%5C(?:%5C|%22|[ntrbf])|[A-Za-z0-9_.-]|%(?:[0-13-46-9A-F][0-9A-F]|5[0-9ABD-F]|2[0-9A-F]))*
BADESC <- (?:[A-Zac-egh-mo-qsu-z0-9_.-]|%(?:[0-13-46-9A-F][0-9A-F]|5[0-9ABD-F]|2[0-13-9A-F]))
DQRAW <- (?:%5C(?:%[0-9A-F]{2}|[A-Za-z0-9_.-])|[A-Za-z0-9_.-]|%(?:[0-13-46-9A-F][0-9A-F]|5[0-9ABD-F]|2[0-13-9A-F]))*
SQRAW <- (?:%5C(?:%[0-9A-F]{2}|[A-Za-z0-9_.-])|[A-Za-z0-9_.-]|%(?:[0-13-46-9A-F][0-9A-F]|5[0-9ABD-F]|2[0-689A-F]))*
BADKW <- as|assert|async|await|break|case|class|continue|del|except|finally|for|from|global|import|in|is|lambda|match|nonlocal|raise|try|type|while|with|yield
BOUND <- (?:(?:%[0-9A-F]{2}|[^A-Za-z0-9_])$PCT)?

UNESC<(?<s>$PCT)> ::! unescape s
ESC<(?<s>$PCT)> ::! escape s
GE<(?<a>[0-9]),(?<b>[0-9])> ::! ge a b
ADD<(?<a>[0-9]+),(?<b>[0-9]+)> ::! add a b
SUB<(?<a>[0-9]+),(?<b>[0-9]+)> ::! sub a b
EQQ<(?<a>[0-9]+),(?<b>[0-9]+)> ::! eq a b
GTT<(?<a>[0-9]+),(?<b>[0-9]+)> ::! gt a b

String bodies are checked before a token is emitted. A bad escape is not an unclosed quote.
